## Feature 3: Hiring Manager Guest Portal

### 3A. DB Migration — `supabase/migrations/20260408300000_add_guest_links.sql`

```sql
CREATE TABLE public.guest_links (
  id          uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  job_id      uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES public.jobs(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  team_id     uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES public.teams(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  token       text NOT NULL UNIQUE DEFAULT encode(gen_random_bytes(32), 'hex'),
  created_by  uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  label       text,
  access_level text NOT NULL DEFAULT 'read' CHECK (access_level IN ('read')),
  expires_at  timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT (now() + interval '30 days'),
  revoked     boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
  created_at  timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE INDEX idx_guest_links_token ON public.guest_links(token);
CREATE INDEX idx_guest_links_job ON public.guest_links(job_id);

ALTER TABLE public.guest_links ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Team admins/owners can manage guest links
CREATE POLICY "Team admins can view guest links"
  ON public.guest_links FOR SELECT TO authenticated
  USING (public.is_team_admin(auth.uid(), team_id) OR created_by = auth.uid());

CREATE POLICY "Team admins can create guest links"
  ON public.guest_links FOR INSERT TO authenticated
  WITH CHECK (public.is_team_admin(auth.uid(), team_id) OR public.is_team_member(auth.uid(), team_id));

CREATE POLICY "Team admins can update guest links"
  ON public.guest_links FOR UPDATE TO authenticated
  USING (public.is_team_admin(auth.uid(), team_id) OR created_by = auth.uid());
```

### 3B. Edge Function — `supabase/functions/guest-portal/index.ts`

Follow the CORS pattern from `send-team-invite/index.ts` but allow all origins (public endpoint like `submit-application`).

```typescript
import { serve } from "https://deno.land/std@0.168.0/http/server.ts";
import { createClient } from "https://esm.sh/@supabase/supabase-js@2";

const corsHeaders = {
  "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": "*",
  "Access-Control-Allow-Headers": "authorization, x-client-info, apikey, content-type",
};

serve(async (req) => {
  if (req.method === "OPTIONS") return new Response("ok", { headers: corsHeaders });

  try {
    const url = new URL(req.url);
    const token = url.searchParams.get("token");
    if (!token) return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "Token required" }), { status: 400, headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" } });

    const supabase = createClient(
      Deno.env.get("SUPABASE_URL")!,
      Deno.env.get("SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY")!
    );

    // Look up guest link
    const { data: link, error: linkError } = await supabase
      .from("guest_links")
      .select("*")
      .eq("token", token)
      .single();

    if (linkError || !link) return errorResponse("Link not found", 404);
    if (link.revoked) return errorResponse("This link has been revoked", 403);
    if (new Date(link.expires_at) < new Date()) return errorResponse("This link has expired", 403);

    // Get job info
    const { data: job } = await supabase
      .from("jobs")
      .select("id, title, location, department")
      .eq("id", link.job_id)
      .single();

    if (!job) return errorResponse("Job not found", 404);

    // Get candidates with scores — sanitized, NO PII (no email, phone)
    const { data: resumes } = await supabase
      .from("resumes")
      .select("id, candidate_name, status")
      .eq("job_id", link.job_id)
      .eq("status", "done");

    // Get results for these resumes
    const resumeIds = (resumes ?? []).map((r: any) => r.id);
    const { data: results } = resumeIds.length > 0
      ? await supabase.from("results").select("resume_id, overall_score, explanation_json").in("resume_id", resumeIds)
      : { data: [] };

    // Get candidate stages
    const { data: stages } = resumeIds.length > 0
      ? await supabase.from("candidate_stages").select("resume_id, stage").in("resume_id", resumeIds)
      : { data: [] };

    // Merge data
    const resultsMap = Object.fromEntries((results ?? []).map((r: any) => [r.resume_id, r]));
    const stagesMap = Object.fromEntries((stages ?? []).map((s: any) => [s.resume_id, s.stage]));

    const candidates = (resumes ?? []).map((r: any) => ({
      name: r.candidate_name || "Unknown",
      score: resultsMap[r.id]?.overall_score ?? null,
      stage: stagesMap[r.id] ?? "new",
      summary: resultsMap[r.id]?.explanation_json?.summary ?? null,
    })).sort((a: any, b: any) => (b.score ?? 0) - (a.score ?? 0));

    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ job: { title: job.title, location: job.location, department: job.department }, candidates }), {
      headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    });
  } catch (err) {
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "Internal server error" }), { status: 500, headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" } });
  }
});
```

### 3C. Public Page — `src/pages/SharedPortal.tsx`

Route: `/shared/:token` — public, no auth required.

Follow the pattern from `src/pages/Apply.tsx` for the public page layout (no SidebarLayout, standalone page with Rankora branding).

- On mount, fetch from edge function: `supabase.functions.invoke("guest-portal", { body: null, headers: {} })` — actually, since it's GET with query params, use fetch directly:
  ```typescript
  const res = await fetch(`${import.meta.env.VITE_SUPABASE_URL}/functions/v1/guest-portal?token=${token}`, {
    headers: { apikey: import.meta.env.VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY },
  });
  ```

- Show job title, location, department in header
- Candidate list as cards or table rows:
  - Name | Score (progress bar, colored by score range) | Stage (badge) | Summary snippet
  - Sorted by score descending
- "Powered by Rankora" footer
- Error states: "Link not found", "Link expired", "Link revoked" — each with appropriate icon and message
- Loading: skeleton cards
- Mobile-first, clean design

### 3D. Guest Link Dialog — `src/components/GuestLinkDialog.tsx`

A dialog component for creating/managing guest links for a specific job.

Props:
```typescript
interface GuestLinkDialogProps {
  open: boolean;
  onOpenChange: (open: boolean) => void;
  jobId: string;
  teamId: string;
}
```

Content:
- Header: "Share with Hiring Manager"
- List of existing active (non-revoked, non-expired) guest links for this job
  - Each shows: label (or "Untitled"), expiry date, copy URL button, revoke button
  - Fetch via `(supabase as any).from("guest_links").select("*").eq("job_id", jobId).eq("revoked", false).order("created_at", { ascending: false })`
- "Generate new link" section:
  - Optional label input (placeholder: "e.g., For VP Engineering")
  - Generate button
  - On click: insert into guest_links with job_id, team_id, created_by (from useAuth)
  - On success: toast "Guest link created" + copy URL to clipboard automatically
- Copy URL format: `${window.location.origin}/shared/${link.token}`
- Revoke: update `revoked = true`, toast "Link revoked"

Use Dialog/DialogContent/DialogHeader from shadcn-ui.

### 3E. Router + JobDetailView Integration

**Modify `src/App.tsx`:**
- Add lazy import: `const SharedPortal = lazy(() => import("./pages/SharedPortal"));`
- Add public route alongside `/apply/:jobId`: `<Route path="/shared/:token" element={<SharedPortal />} />`

**Modify `src/components/JobDetailView.tsx`:**
- Import `GuestLinkDialog` and `Share2` icon from lucide-react
- Add state: `const [showGuestLink, setShowGuestLink] = useState(false);`
- Find the area near the existing "Copy Apply Link" button in the job header
- Add a "Share" button next to it:
  ```tsx
  <Button variant="outline" size="sm" className="gap-1.5" onClick={() => setShowGuestLink(true)}>
    <Share2 className="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
    Share
  </Button>
  ```
- Render the dialog: `<GuestLinkDialog open={showGuestLink} onOpenChange={setShowGuestLink} jobId={jobId} teamId={teamId} />`
- Get teamId from the job data or from useTeam hook. Read JobDetailView carefully to find how to get the team_id — the job object may already have it, or you may need to add a small query.

---

## Critical constraints:
- NEVER edit `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts`
- Use `(supabase as any)` for all tables not in generated types (guest_links, candidate_notes with mentions column, activity_log)
- Import from `@/` path alias always
- Use shadcn-ui components only from `src/components/ui/`
- Sonner `toast.success()` / `toast.error()` for notifications
- Run `npm run build` at the end to verify zero TypeScript errors
- Public pages (SharedPortal) must NOT use SidebarLayout or ProtectedRoute

